<!-- Buying guide (unique local copy; facts from this page, manufacturer spec pages, and /guides/) -->
<section class="pt-70 pb-30">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="row justify-content-center">
      <div class="col-lg-9 guide-body">
        <h2>Who the ALL-IN-110V Series is for</h2>
        <p>The ALL-IN-110V Series is for anyone who wants a real Nordic hot tub without electrical work: renters, townhome owners, first-time buyers, and anyone whose panel is far from the backyard. These aren't stripped-down tubs. Nordic Wrap insulation and the Nordic Clean ozonator are standard, along with Nordic Star stainless jets and LED lighting. Choose from rectangles (Retreat, Stella), the heart-shaped D'Amour for two, or round tubs (Warrior XL, Crown, Sport).</p>
        <h2>How plug-and-play works</h2>
        <p>Every ALL-IN-110V model plugs into a standard 110V outlet with a <strong>factory-installed GFCI cord</strong>. They run a 1 hp, two-speed pump and a 1 kW heater. The trade-off is heating speed: a 1 kW heater raises about 300 gallons by roughly 1.4°F per hour before heat loss, so do the first fill a day ahead and keep the cover on between soaks. The entry-level Sport, for example, holds about 280 gallons and has 15 jets. Our <a href="/guides/110v-vs-240v-hot-tubs/">110V vs 240V guide</a> explains the trade-offs in detail.</p>
        <h2>ALL-IN-110V in a Utah winter</h2>
        <p>Standard Nordic Wrap insulation helps a lot here, since it's the upgrade Nordic says adds R-9.5 for cold climates. Keep the spa full, powered and covered, and expect slower recovery after a long soak with the lid off. See our <a href="/guides/hot-tub-utah-winter/">winter guide</a>. Placement is flexible, but the spa still needs a level, solid base, and HomeGuide's national data puts a concrete pad at $500–$2,500.</p>
        <h2>See ALL-IN-110V models in Midvale</h2>
        <p>We keep display models from every brand we carry at 6905 S State St in Midvale (Mon–Sat, 10 AM–5 PM). Floor models change, so <a href="/contact/">call or message us</a> if you want to sit in a specific model before you visit.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

